       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB231NATW.
      *> kb/Work PB231 - THE OTHER THREE SURFACES OF THE ONE BYTE-
      *> WINDOW CARRIAGE GATE OVER A NATIONAL LEAF: REDEFINES, THE
      *> IN-CLASS OCCURS STRIDE, AND THE EXTERNAL RUN-UNIT CELL. THE
      *> BASED/ALLOCATE SURFACE IS 2002/pb231_based_national_leaf; ALL
      *> FOUR ROUTE THROUGH DataBinder.ByteWindowResidueOf AND
      *> ByteWindowResidueDriftTests PINS THAT THEY AGREE.
      *> THE LAW BEING OBSERVED: A SHARED STORAGE AREA IS BYTE-
      *> ADDRESSED, SO A MEMBER OCCUPIES ITS STORAGE EXTENT AND NOT ITS
      *> CHARACTER-POSITION COUNT. 13.18.44.4 GR1 SAYS SO IN SO MANY
      *> WORDS - "STORAGE ASSOCIATION FOR THE SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY
      *> STARTS AT THE FIRST BIT OF THE DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY
      *> data-name-2 AND CONTINUES OVER AN AREA SUFFICIENT TO CONTAIN
      *> THE NUMBER OF BITS REQUIRED BY THE DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY THE
      *> SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY" - AND 13.18.60.4 GR8 MAKES A NATIONAL
      *> CHARACTER'S SIZE THE IMPLEMENTOR'S; COBOL.NET PINS TWO BYTES,
      *> UTF-16BE (D-N1).
      *> (1) REDEFINES. C IS PIC X(8); D REDEFINES IT AS PIC N(4),
      *> WHICH IS EIGHT BYTES - THE SAME AREA. 13.18.44.4 GR2: "WHEN
      *> THE SAME STORAGE AREA IS DEFINED BY MORE THAN ONE DATA
      *> DESCRIPTION ENTRY, THE DATA-NAME ASSOCIATED WITH ANY OF THOSE
      *> DATA DESCRIPTION ENTRIES MAY BE USED TO REFERENCE THAT STORAGE
      *> AREA." MOVE N"WXYZ" TO D THEN SHOWS THROUGH C AS THE FOUR
      *> UTF-16BE PAIRS 00 57 / 00 58 / 00 59 / 00 5A. FUNCTION ORD IS
      *> THE BYTE VALUE + 1 (15.70.1 - "THE LOWEST ORDINAL POSITION IS
      *> 1"), SO BYTE 0 = 0x00 -> 1, BYTE 1 = 0x57 = 87 -> 88, AND
      *> BYTE 7 = 0x5A = 90 -> 91. A CHARACTER-POSITION READ WOULD HAVE
      *> PUT "WXYZ" IN BYTES 0-3 AND LEFT 4-7 UNTOUCHED.
      *> (2) THE IN-CLASS OCCURS STRIDE. KT IS PIC N(2) OCCURING 3, SO
      *> EACH OCCURRENCE IS FOUR BYTES AND OCCURRENCE 2 STARTS AT BYTE
      *> 4 - KX(5:1) AND KX(6:1) ARE ITS FIRST PAIR. 13.18.44 LAYS THE
      *> OCCURRENCES END TO END IN THE ONE BACKING; A TWO-BYTE STRIDE
      *> WOULD HAVE PUT OCCURRENCE 2 AT BYTE 2 AND OVERLAPPED
      *> OCCURRENCE 1. N"AB" IS 00 41 00 42, SO KX(5:1) -> ORD 1,
      *> KX(6:1) -> ORD 66, KX(7:1) -> ORD 1, KX(8:1) -> ORD 67, AND
      *> OCCURRENCE 1 (KX(1:4)) IS STILL THE NATIONAL SPACES THE
      *> INITIAL STATE GAVE IT: 00 20 00 20 -> ORD 1 33.
      *> (3) THE EXTERNAL RUN-UNIT CELL (13.18.22 - ONE STORAGE COPY
      *> PER NAME PER RUN UNIT). A NATIONAL LEAF AND AN ALPHANUMERIC
      *> LEAF SHARE THE SAME CELL AND EACH READS BACK ITS OWN VALUE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 H.
          05 C PIC X(8).
          05 D REDEFINES C PIC N(4).
       01 K.
          05 KT PIC N(2) OCCURS 3.
       01 KX REDEFINES K PIC X(12).
       01 E EXTERNAL.
          05 E-N PIC N(2).
          05 E-X PIC X(2).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE N"WXYZ" TO D
           DISPLAY "D=[" D "]"
           DISPLAY "CORD=" FUNCTION ORD(C(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(C(2:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(C(7:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(C(8:1))
           MOVE N"AB" TO KT(2)
           DISPLAY "KT2=[" KT(2) "]"
           DISPLAY "KORD=" FUNCTION ORD(KX(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(KX(2:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(KX(5:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(KX(6:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(KX(7:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(KX(8:1))
           MOVE N"PQ" TO E-N
           MOVE "RS" TO E-X
           DISPLAY "E-N=[" E-N "] E-X=[" E-X "]"
           STOP RUN.
